{
  "season": 1,
  "week": 17,
  "articles": [
    {
      "id": "injury-report-s1-w17",
      "type": "feature",
      "author": "tessa-wren",
      "title": "Injury Report: playoff offenses lose Holt, Gyarzalez, Oinkologne and Tatsugiri",
      "dek": "The final-round availability report covers new absences, recovery countdowns and cleared remaining weeks across the league.",
      "teams": [],
      "body": [
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "The final regular-season week arrives with new absences for several playoff clubs. Mossdeep’s Poury Holt is out seven reported weeks, Mt. Silver’s Tony Gyarzalez six, Petalburg’s Oinkologne three and Eterna quarterback Tatsugiri seven. Canalave, still pursuing the last wild card, has lost Nidoking for nine weeks and Seismitoad for six. These are current reported durations, not confirmed return dates."
        },
        {
          "type": "h2",
          "text": "Contenders must replace productive work"
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Holt ran for 115 yards in Mossdeep’s 22–3 win and caught a five-yard pass. The Eclipse have already secured the first seed and bye, but that protection in the bracket does not supply his rushing production. Shawn Mareman contributed forty-eight yards on eight carries in the same game, an observed alternative contribution rather than an announced future assignment. Richard Furman’s remaining absence has reached zero, although his injured-reserve status still requires a separate roster decision."
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Gyarzalez caught five passes for fifty-six yards while Crem Ftzpatrik threw for 318 in Mt. Silver’s win at Azalea. The Reds also have a new two-week absence for Ninjask. Their bye is secured, allowing preparation time after the finale, but neither duration establishes who will be available in a particular playoff game. Foo Warner’s remaining absence has reached zero."
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Petalburg secured Hoenn West while Oinkologne generated eighty-nine rushing yards on five carries and thirty receiving yards. His three-week designation removes a substantial part of the offense that beat Rustboro. Whiscash had twelve carries for minus-two yards in that game. Seviper’s previous one-week absence has reached zero, providing a useful receiving-status change while leaving the future lineup unconfirmed."
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Eterna’s new seven-week designation for Tatsugiri changes the preparation for a division champion. Stantler is also out two weeks. The Thorns have won with a low-scoring profile and a defense that has allowed 181 points through sixteen games; the available offense must now be reassessed for Snowpoint and the coming home playoff game. No replacement start is announced by this report."
        },
        {
          "type": "h2",
          "text": "The last-berth races have changed personnel"
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Canalave beat Snowpoint 24–21 with sixty rushing yards from Nidoking, who now has a nine-week absence. Seismitoad is out six weeks. Delcatty contributed forty-five rushing yards in the win, but that does not establish a complete replacement plan for the trip to Oreburgh. Canalave must win and receive help from Mauville’s result to guarantee the final berth."
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Olivine’s Gogoat is out five weeks after the 10–3 loss to Cianwood. Bibarel’s remaining absence has reached zero. The Ironclads still qualify by beating Azalea, so the backfield changes arrive before a game they can use to settle the race themselves. Violet’s Zangoose, who ran for fifty-one yards against Lavender, is out four weeks before the Falcons host Mahogany."
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Cianwood’s Gardevoir has reached zero remaining weeks. That is a meaningful quarterback availability update after Swampert completed three of twelve passes in the win over Olivine. It does not confirm Gardevoir’s activation, starting role or appearance against Mt. Silver. Haunter continues with two reported weeks out. Cerulean’s Watchog has a new eighteen-week designation before the Tide’s must-win game with Vermilion."
        },
        {
          "type": "h2",
          "text": "The Johto East decider and other returns"
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Blackthorn’s Exploud has a new two-week absence after rushing for thirty-seven yards against Mahogany. Sawsbuck remains out five weeks. Lavender’s Mr. Clanky continues at six weeks, while People Eater has reached zero remaining weeks. Moth Ball’s five-touchdown performance establishes what the available quarterback did against Violet; it does not establish the injured starter’s return."
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Cinnabar’s Seismitoad has reached zero remaining weeks, while Arcanine remains out two and Octillery one. Other cleared remaining absences include Fortree’s Pawmot, Mahogany’s Jellicent, Lavaridge’s Mantine, Azalea’s Castform and Celadon’s Anorith. A countdown reaching zero differs from a recorded game appearance. The table retains both new entries and ordinary recovery changes so those developments are not conflated."
        },
